From: Dragos Cosmin <zahariadragoscosmin@hotmail.com>
Subject: net: ethernet: cortina: don't use the TSS bypass for full-size frames

On a Raidsonic IB-4210-B (SL3512, RTL8211B, 1 Gbps) the TX DMA stops
permanently within seconds of sending full-size (1514 byte) non-TCP
frames, e.g. "ping -s 1472": the hardware read pointer freezes on a
descriptor with TSS_BYPASS_BIT set, the queue fills up and only a reboot
recovers. With 1400 byte frames the same load (plus TCP in both
directions) runs clean.

The bypass was meant for frames *bigger* than 1514 bytes, but the test
used >= ETH_FRAME_LEN. Use > so ordinary full-size frames take the normal
checksum path again (as the old sl351x driver always did), and for really
oversized frames keep the software checksum but don't set the bypass bit.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Dragos Cosmin <zahariadragoscosmin@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cortina/gemini.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cortina/gemini.c
@@ -1193,21 +1193,25 @@ static int gmac_map_tx_bufs(struct net_d
 			   skb->len, netdev->mtu, mss);
 		word1 |= TSS_MTU_ENABLE_BIT;
 		word3 |= mss;
-	} else if (skb->len >= ETH_FRAME_LEN) {
+	} else if (skb->len > ETH_FRAME_LEN) {
 		/* Hardware offloaded checksumming isn't working on non-TCP frames
 		 * bigger than 1514 bytes. A hypothesis about this is that the
 		 * checksum buffer is only 1518 bytes, so when the frames get
 		 * bigger they get truncated, or the last few bytes get
 		 * overwritten by the FCS.
 		 *
-		 * Just use software checksumming and bypass on bigger frames.
+		 * Just use software checksumming on bigger frames. Do not set
+		 * TSS_BYPASS_BIT: on the SL3512 (Raidsonic IB-4210-B) a
+		 * full-size frame with the bypass bit set stops the TX DMA
+		 * for good (read pointer frozen, only a reboot recovers).
+		 * A plain 1514 byte frame is handled fine by the checksum
+		 * engine, as the old OpenWrt sl351x driver always did.
 		 */
 		if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL) {
 			ret = skb_checksum_help(skb);
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
 		}
-		word1 |= TSS_BYPASS_BIT;
 	}
 
 	if (skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL) {
